SUMMARY:Teaching As Art Practice | Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T163000
DTSTAMP:20260707T142801Z
UID:20260711T223000Z-21518@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T153000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,703,703/629_cs_-_Teaching_As_Art_Practice.rev.178345
 9658.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events,District Events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an inspiring afternoon at the Petaluma Arts Center
  for Teaching As Art Practice\, a panel discussion exploring the dynamic r
 elationship between teaching and creative practice.  Drawing from Aristotl
 e's quote\, "Those who can\, do\; those who understand\, teach\," this con
 versation brings together artist educators from across the North Bay to di
 scuss how teaching art shapes\, challenges\, and enriches their own artist
 ic work. Through personal experiences and shared perspectives\, panelists 
 will reflect on mentorship\, creative process\, pedagogy\, and the evolvin
 g role of educators within contemporary art communities.  The panel featur
 es professors and teachers from Sonoma State University\, College of Marin
 \, and Santa Rosa Junior College.  Moderated by New Voices Curator Emma Lo
 gan\, this engaging discussion offers insight into the intersection of art
 making\, education\, and community connection.For more information and tic
 kets\, visit their website here. (https://www.petalumaartscenter.org/event
 s-exhibitions/new-voices-menrh)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260707T212801Z
LOCATION:230 Lakeville Street Petaluma\, CA
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/21518-teaching-as-art-practice-pa
 nel-discussion
