 e Petaluma Arts Center for <em>Teaching As Art Practice</em>\, a panel dis
 cussion exploring the dynamic relationship between teaching and creative p
 ractice.</p><p>  Drawing from Aristotle's quote\, "Those who can\, do\; th
 ose who understand\, teach\," this conversation brings together artist edu
 cators from across the North Bay to discuss how teaching art shapes\, chal
 lenges\, and enriches their own artistic work. Through personal experience
 s and shared perspectives\, panelists will reflect on mentorship\, creativ
 e process\, pedagogy\, and the evolving role of educators within contempor
 ary art communities.</p><p>  The panel features professors and teachers fr
 om Sonoma State University\, College of Marin\, and Santa Rosa Junior Coll
 ege.</p><p>  Moderated by New Voices Curator Emma Logan\, this engaging di
 scussion offers insight into the intersection of artmaking\, education\, a
 nd community connection.</p><p><a href="https://www.petalumaartscenter.org
 /events-exhibitions/new-voices-menrh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For m
 ore information and tickets\, visit their website here.</a></p>
