 using on the three essential elements of successful artwork: drawing\, val
 ue\, and color. In this two-day workshop\, George will guide students thro
 ugh the fundamentals of composition and drawing\, including how to create 
 a strong focal point\, measure proportions accurately\, and lead the viewe
 r's eye through a painting. Next\, participants will explore the critical 
 role of value by painting with only Ultramarine Blue and White\, learning 
 how light and dark relationships create depth\, form\, and visual impact. 
 Finally\, students will unlock the secrets of color harmony using only the
  three primary colors and white\, mixing a wide range of vibrant palettes 
 while exploring warm and cool color relationships\, color temperature\, an
 d atmospheric perspective. Through demonstrations and a series of color st
 udies\, this workshop provides artists of all levels with practical tools 
 for creating stronger\, more confident paintings. Materials A supply list 
 will be provided upon signup. Provided: table easels This class is located
  in the PAC classroom.&nbsp\; Two days\, 12-4PM each day. About the Teache
 r:&nbsp\; George Scribner i s an artist\, filmmaker\, and longtime Disney 
 animator\, director\, and fine artist with more than 35 years at The Walt 
 Disney Company. Born and raised in Panama\, he directed Disney's animated 
 feature&nbsp\; Oliver &amp\; Company &nbsp\;and has earned international r
 ecognition for his large-scale documentary paintings. His major commission
 s include creating 35 oil paintings chronicling the expansion of the Panam
 a Canal for its permanent collection and a multi-year series documenting t
 he construction of Shanghai Disneyland. Through his work\, George combines
  masterful draftsmanship\, storytelling\, and a lifelong passion for paint
 ing and animation. Learn More:&nbsp\; www.scribnerart.com #block-aba766277
